@startuml deployment-diagram
/'
AI Usage Note
Drafted with Claude from high-level-design.md §6 and the team's architecture decisions.
Layout checked by rendering with PlantUML; reviewed by Daryna Halytska.
'/
title Nearby — Deployment Diagram with Trust Boundaries

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 70
skinparam ranksep 80

rectangle "Z0 · Internet — untrusted" as Z0 #FFF5F5;line:B71C1C;line.dashed {
  node "User device\n(iOS / Android / browser)" as dev {
    artifact "Expo app\nCMP-01" as app
  }
}

rectangle "Our infrastructure" as INFRA #FAFAFA;line:424242 {

  rectangle "Z1 · Edge" as Z1 #FFFDE7;line:F9A825;line.dashed {
    node "Load balancer /\nreverse proxy" as lb
  }

  rectangle "Z2 · Core — trusted" as Z2 #F1F8E9;line:2E7D32;line.dashed {
    node "App host" as host_main {
      artifact "Main server\nCMP-02 (NestJS)\n1 instance, scales horizontally" as main
    }
    node "Secrets store\nJWT, column-encryption\nand HMAC keys" as secrets
  }

  rectangle "Z3 · Import — partly trusted\n(parses untrusted input)" as Z3 #FFF3E0;line:E65100;line.dashed {
    node "App host (import)" as host_import {
      artifact "Event import service\nCMP-03 (NestJS)" as imp
    }
  }

  rectangle "Z4 · Data — trusted" as Z4 #E3F2FD;line:1565C0;line.dashed {
    database "Managed PostgreSQL\nCMP-04\nencrypted volume, daily backups\npg-boss queue, profile photos" as db
  }
}

rectangle "Z5 · External services — outside our control" as Z5 #F3E5F5;line:6A1B9A;line.dashed {
  node "Event providers\n(Concert.ua, ArtWizard)\nEXT-01" as providers
  node "Telegram Gateway API / SMS\nEXT-03" as tg
  node "Expo Push\nEXT-02" as push
  node "Google\nEXT-04" as google
}

app --> lb : **TB1**\nHTTPS (TLS 1.2+)
lb --> main : **TB2**\nprivate network
main --> db : **TB3**\nSQL, role nearby_main
imp --> db : **TB4**\nSQL, role nearby_import
imp --> providers : **TB5**\nHTTPS pull\n(untrusted data)
main --> tg : **TB6**\nverification codes
main --> push : **TB6**\npush batches
main --> google : **TB6**\nID token check
main --> secrets : **TB7**\nkeys
push ..> app : push\n(no contacts)

legend right
  Dashed frames are trust zones; **TB1–TB7** mark the boundaries
  analysed in threat-model.md §1–§2.
  TB1  device ↔ load balancer / API
  TB3, TB4  server processes ↔ PostgreSQL
  TB5, TB6  our infrastructure ↔ external services
  TB2, TB7  internal boundaries inside our infrastructure
endlegend

@enduml